# Secondary Structure Prediction

## Overview

Secondary structure prediction is the process of identifying the local structural elements of a protein from its amino acid sequence.
It predicts the arrangement of α-helices, β-strands, and random coils, providing insights into protein folding and serving as an important
step toward tertiary structure prediction. In this project, PSIPRED was used for secondary structure prediction.

## Objective

To predict the secondary structural elements of the target protein and understand its structural organization.

## Methodology

The protein sequence in FASTA format was submitted to the PSIPRED server, which analyzed the sequence and predicted the positions of
α-helices, β-strands, and random coils along with confidence scores.

## Input

* Protein sequence (FASTA).

## Output

* Predicted α-helices, β-strands, and coils.
* Confidence scores.
* Graphical representation of the secondary structure.

## Applications

* Protein structure analysis.
* Function prediction.
* Support for tertiary structure prediction.
* Comparative protein studies.

## Files Included

* Protein sequence (FASTA).
* PSIPRED prediction results.

## Conclusion

Secondary structure prediction identified the structural elements of the target protein, providing valuable insights into its folding
pattern and supporting subsequent tertiary structure prediction and structural analysis.

